# Text is text everywhere: LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Why a blanket rule and not one line per file: this repository is generated,
# so the file list grows on its own. `LATEST` was already outside the list and
# every `git add` warned about it. A rule that has to be extended by hand is a
# rule that will be forgotten -- the project this engine pilots learned that
# the expensive way (841 files converted on checkout, 814 of them reported as
# unformatted, and gate criteria that matched on one machine and not another).
#
# `core.autocrlf` cannot do this job: it binds one machine, this file binds
# everyone who clones, and it overrides that setting.
#
# The two `binary` lines below come AFTER this rule on purpose: they win, and
# the published binaries keep the bytes their checksum was taken over.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The published binaries are bytes, not text: an end-of-line conversion on
# checkout would change the file this repository publishes a checksum for.
x3-windows-amd64.exe binary
x3-linux-amd64 binary

*.md text eol=lf
SHA256SUMS.txt text eol=lf
